{
  "total_prepetition_claim": 125000,
  "admin_503b9": {
    "amount": 78100,
    "invoices": ["MS-7788", "MS-7815"]
  },
  "general_unsecured": 46900,
  "reclamation": {
    "available": true,
    "why": "Three goods invoices were received by Redwood while insolvent within 45 days before the 2026-03-10 petition (window opens 2026-01-24): MS-7740 (rec. 2026-02-04, unpaid balance 25,600), MS-7788 (rec. 2026-02-20, 41,300), MS-7815 (rec. 2026-03-04, 36,800) — 103,700 of goods on which nothing remains to be paid beyond that balance. §546(c)(1) requires WRITTEN demand no later than 45 days after receipt; for MS-7740 that date (2026-03-21) falls after commencement, so the later 20-days-after-petition rule governs: demand must be served on or before 2026-03-30 (11 days from today). No demand appears in the file. CAVEATS: (a) reclamation is subject to the DIP lender's blanket lien (library note to bc_546c) so the reclamation right is likely of little or no real value — assert it to preserve leverage; (b) insolvency at each receipt is assumed from the chapter 11 filing, not yet proven; (c) traceability of identifiable goods is assumed, not in the file. MS-7701 (rec. 2026-01-14) is outside the 45-day window and was paid in full."
  },
  "bar_date": "2026-06-11",
  "preference": {
    "transfers_in_90_days": 180000,
    "ordinary_course_defense": {
      "protected": 95000,
      "exposed": 85000,
      "reasoning": "90-day window opens 2025-12-10. Four payments: 2025-12-18 $51,000 (45 days after invoice, ACH), 2026-01-22 $44,000 (43 days, ACH) — both match the parties' 12-month history of 8 payments at 43-47 days by ACH, so §547(c)(2)(A) should protect them (95,000). 2026-02-10 $48,200 (29 days, ACH) was paid under Mesa's unilateral 2026-01-20 terms change to NET 15 with oldest-first application — payment speed diverges from the parties' history, and shortened terms/pressure fall outside (c)(2)(A); 2026-02-27 $36,800 (partial, by WIRE demanded by Mesa's credit manager) is an unusual method vs. an all-ACH history — both exposed (85,000). (c)(2)(B) 'ordinary business terms' (industry standard) was not tested; no industry evidence in file. Creditor bears the burden on (c) defenses, §547(g)."
    },
    "new_value_defense": 85000,
    "net_exposure_estimate": 0
  },
  "stay_violations": [
    "2026-03-12: 'FINAL NOTICE — pay $210,000 within 5 days or we refer to collections' letter, mailed and emailed — an act to collect a pre-petition claim, §362(a)(6) (library bc_362.md: dunning letters after petition are acts to collect).",
    "2026-03-15: collection call to Redwood AP after the petition; AP told Mesa 'we filed Chapter 11, talk to counsel'; Mesa's AR clerk replied 'that's not our problem, you owe us' — continued collection attempt, and from this date Mesa had actual knowledge, making later violations willful under §362(k).",
    "2026-03-18: email to Redwood CFO threatening to 'hold all future shipments and report to credit bureaus' — threats to report to credit bureaus after the petition are acts to collect (library bc_362.md); §362(k) liability for willful violations includes actual damages, costs and attorneys' fees, and punitive damages in appropriate circumstances; courts also sanction creditors for willful violations under §105 (library bc_362.md). The shipment-withholding threat is not squarely addressed in the library — flagged unverified."
  ],
  "immediate_actions": [
    "STOP ALL COLLECTION TODAY (hard stop directive to AR dept, in writing): no more letters, calls, credit-bureau reports or threats — each is a §362(a)(6) violation and Mesa is already on notice of the case, so any further act is willful under §362(k).",
    "Serve a WRITTEN reclamation demand under §546(c)(1) on or before 2026-03-30 covering MS-7740, MS-7788, MS-7788/MS-7815 goods (103,700 unpaid value); likely subordinated to the DIP blanket lien but preserves leverage.",
    "Contact debtor's counsel immediately re: the pending critical-vendor motion (Dkt. 44), hearing 2026-04-02 — notice says creditors wishing to be considered must contact debtor's counsel; expect to agree to customary trade terms for the case (library critical_vendor_practice.md).",
    "File Proof of Claim (Form 410) by the bar date 2026-06-11, 5:00 p.m. MT, via the claims agent's e-filing — file asserts 78,100 as §503(b)(9) administrative and 46,900 general unsecured (per library frbp_3002_3003.md, the 503(b)(9) portion must be asserted separately from the GUC claim by the procedure the bar-date order specifies).",
    "Do NOT set off or withhold payments against Redwood without stay relief — setoff of pre-petition mutual debts requires relief from the automatic stay (library bc_502d_setoff.md).",
    "Quantify and reserve for preference exposure: gross exposure up to 85,000 on the two non-ordinary-course payments; new-value defense likely erases it (net estimate 0; worst case ~36,800, see proof memo) — under §502(d) the court can disallow Mesa's ENTIRE claim until any preference liability is paid, so this must be settled or resolved before distribution.",
    "Preserve all documents (emails, AR notes, shipment and lien records); identify who at Mesa knew of the filing and when (the 3/15 call) — relevant to willfulness.",
    "Decide supply posture deliberately: continued ordinary-course shipments support the critical-vendor case; do not condition them on payment of pre-petition debt (that is itself a collection act)."
  ]
}

